title: Raritan PX2/PX3: Inlet Pole Residual Current
agents: snmp
catalog: hw/environment/raritan
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check reads residual-current and RCM sensors from the PDU2-MIB
 inletPoleSensorMeasurementsTable for each inlet conductor. Whole-inlet
 measurements are handled independently by raritan_pdu_residual_current_summary.

 Combined, AC and DC residual currents have separate metrics. Values and device
 thresholds use the matching sensor's precision and signed/unsigned columns.
 Enabled lower and upper limits and device/RCM states are evaluated. A sole
 active upper device limit X supplies WARN/CRIT X/X; device WARN 0 with active
 CRIT X also uses X/X. Rule values override device limits unchanged, including
 warning zero or explicitly disabled levels. Rules and metrics use amperes;
 service output displays milliamperes.

 The shared residual_current rule controls combined, AC and DC limits and
 missing-data/missing-levels handling. Optional AC/DC values without separate
 levels do not add missing-level warnings when a combined sensor is present.
 The residual-current percentage uses load current from this exact inlet pole.
 No summary is calculated from pole readings.

item:
 The inletLabel followed by Phase and the actual inletPoleLine, e.g.
 {{I1 Phase L2}}. The service name is {{Residual Current I1 Phase L2}}.
 Multiple detected PDUs add their index; duplicate labels/lines are
 disambiguated. Missing labels or line mappings use index-based fallbacks.

discovery:
 One service for each inlet pole with an available residual-current or RCM
 sensor. Configuration or load-current readings alone do not create services.
